        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): strip attachments >10MB before send to prevent HTTP 413 silent message loss (fixes #99021)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #99021.\n\nWhen a Discord media attachment exceeds Discord's 10 MB bot API limit, the entire multipart request (text + file) is rejected with HTTP 413 and silently lost.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n1. **send.outbound.ts**: Added `isDiscordEntityTooLargeError` guard. On 413, re-sends as text-only with size-limit note. Added **forum/media channel** protection — same 413 fallback now applies to forum thread media sends.\n2. **send.shared.ts**: `effectiveMaxBytes = maxBytes ?? 10MB`\n3. **send.receipt.ts**: Added `mediaStripped` flag so callers classify stripped-media receipts as text.\n4. **4 regression tests** (normal 413 + forum 413 + mediaMaxMb respected + text-only long reply) — **46 total**.\n5. **_proof_413.sh**, **_proof_production.mjs**: Mock and real-Discord API proof scripts.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Production path — OpenClaw sendMessageDiscord via real Discord\n\n```\nHost: LIN-66D8BD4EA2C\nTime: 2026-07-03T04:07:46Z\n\n--- Step 1: Send media via patched sendMessageDiscord ---\nMessage ID: 1522453819160531059  ✅\n\n--- Step 2: Text-only send via same path ---\nMessage ID: 1522453826018213918  ✅\n\n=== RESULT: OpenClaw send path works with real Discord API ===\n```\n\n### Raw API — 413 + text fallback (curl)\n\n```\n--- Step 1: 11MB file -> HTTP 413 ---\nHTTP 413  ✅ Discord blocked oversized file\n\n--- Step 2: Text fallback -> HTTP 200 ---\nHTTP 200  ✅ Message delivered\n\n=== RESULT: PASS ===\n```\n\n### Unit tests (46/46 passed)\n\n| Scenario | Result |\n|---------|--------|\n| >10MB attachment -> text-only fallback (normal channel) | ✅ |\n| mediaMaxMb:50 -> 15MB file sent normally | ✅ |\n| >10MB attachment -> text-only fallback (forum channel) | ✅ |\n| Text-only fallback preserves reply text | ✅ |\n\n## AI Assistance\n- AI-assisted: Yes",
